#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:201
msgid "Literal Application"
msgstr "Letterlijke toepassing"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:205
msgid "Context"
msgstr "Context"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:212
msgid "Group"
msgstr "Groep"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:213
msgid "Person categories"
msgstr "Van toepassing op persoonscategorieen"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:214
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/listing.html:156
msgid "Application"
msgstr "Toepassing"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:215
msgid "Codes"
msgstr "Codes"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:231
msgid "More explanation about the icons and New Covenant Literal Application"
msgstr ""
"Meer uitleg over de pictogrammen en de letterlijke toepassing van het Nieuwe"
" Verbond"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:233
msgid ""
"The New Covenant Literal Application Code (NCLA) is an interpretive guide "
"used by the authors to indicate which person categories a mitzvah applies "
"to, and at what level of literal compliance."
msgstr ""
"De code voor letterlijke toepassing binnen het Nieuwe Verbond (NCLA) is een "
"interpretatieve leidraad die door de auteurs wordt gebruikt om aan te geven "
"op welke persoonscategorieen een mitswa van toepassing is, en op welk niveau"
" van letterlijke naleving."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:234
msgid ""
"Each card above groups one application level such as mandated or optional. "
"The three people icons show whether that application is meant for Jewish, "
"K'rov Yisrael, or Gentile believers, and the male or female symbols show "
"whether it applies to men, women, or both."
msgstr ""
"Elke kaart hierboven groepeert één toepassingsniveau, zoals verplicht of "
"optioneel. De drie personenpictogrammen tonen of die toepassing bedoeld is "
"voor Joodse, K'rov Yisrael- of niet-Joodse gelovigen, en de man- of vrouw-"
"symbolen tonen of het voor mannen, vrouwen of beiden geldt."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:237
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:239
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/listing.html:203
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:277
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:718
msgid "Jewish"
msgstr "Joods"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:240
msgid "Used for instruction directed to Jewish believers."
msgstr "Gebruikt voor instructie die gericht is op Joodse gelovigen."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:244
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:246
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/listing.html:210
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:281
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:719
msgid "K'rov Yisrael"
msgstr "K'rov Yisrael"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:247
msgid ""
"Used for non-Jewish believers living closely with Israel and Torah practice."
msgstr ""
"Gebruikt voor niet-Joodse gelovigen die nauw verbonden leven met Israël en "
"de praktijk van de Thora."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:251
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:253
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/listing.html:217
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:285
#: walkasjesus_app/views/law_of_messiah_view.py:720
msgid "Gentile"
msgstr "Niet-Joods"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:254
msgid ""
"Used for instruction presented as applying to Gentile believers more "
"broadly."
msgstr ""
"Gebruikt voor instructie die breder als toepasselijk voor niet-Joodse "
"gelovigen wordt gepresenteerd."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:260
msgid "Male and female symbols"
msgstr "Symbolen voor man en vrouw"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:261
msgid "These show whether the instruction is directed to men, women, or both."
msgstr "Deze tonen of de instructie gericht is op mannen, vrouwen of beiden."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:265
msgid ""
"This code reflects the authors' interpretive opinion and is provided for "
"prayerful consideration. The icon view is only a visual summary; the "
"detailed codes and source explanation remain available below for careful "
"study."
msgstr ""
"Deze code weerspiegelt de interpretatieve mening van de auteurs en wordt "
"gegeven voor overweging in gebed. De pictogramweergave is alleen een visuele"
" samenvatting; de gedetailleerde codes en bronuitleg blijven hieronder "
"beschikbaar voor zorgvuldige studie."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:268
msgid "Detailed codes"
msgstr "Gedetailleerde codes"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:271
msgid "Read the full explanation from the source"
msgstr "Lees de volledige uitleg bij de bron"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:291
msgid "Key NT Scriptures"
msgstr "Belangrijke NT-schriftgedeelten"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:316
msgid "Key OT Scriptures"
msgstr "Belangrijke OT-schriftgedeelten"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:341
msgid "Supportive NT Scriptures"
msgstr "Ondersteunende NT-schriftgedeelten"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:366
msgid "Supportive OT Scriptures"
msgstr "Ondersteunende OT-schriftgedeelten"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:408
msgid "Rabbi Michael Rudolph"
msgstr "Rabbi Michael Rudolph"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:430
msgid "Rabbi Daniel Juster"
msgstr "Rabbi Daniël Juster"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:452
msgid "Classical commentators"
msgstr "Klassieke commentatoren"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:800
#: walkasjesus_app/views/maimonides_view.py:73
msgid "Maimonides"
msgstr "Maimonides"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:801
msgid ""
"Maimonides (Rabbi Moshe ben Maimon, 12th century) organized all 613 Torah "
"commandments into a structured list. These linked items show where this Law "
"of Messiah commandment overlaps with that classical framework."
msgstr ""
"Maimonides (Rabbi Moshe ben Maimon, 12e eeuw) ordende alle 613 Torah-geboden"
" in een gestructureerde lijst. Deze gekoppelde items tonen waar dit gebod "
"uit de Wet van Christus overlap heeft met dat klassieke kader."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:814
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/maimonides/listing.html:118
msgid "Meir of Rothenburg"
msgstr "Meir van Rothenburg"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:815
msgid ""
"Rabbi Meir of Rothenburg (13th century, Germany) was a leading Talmudic "
"authority. These reference numbers link this commandment to his halachic "
"rulings."
msgstr ""
"Rabbi Meir van Rothenburg (13e eeuw, Duitsland) was een toonaangevende "
"Talmoedische autoriteit. Deze referentienummers koppelen dit gebod aan zijn "
"halachische uitspraken."

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:832
#: walkasjesus_app/templates/maimonides/listing.html:130
msgid "Sefer HaChinuch"
msgstr "Sefer HaChinuch"

#: walkasjesus_app/templates/law_of_messiah/detail.html:833
msgid ""
